Spawn-safe DataLoader workers for the winding dataset (macOS).

Why: train_winding_model.py hard-codes multiprocessing_context="fork". On macOS a
forked worker can abort inside the Objective-C runtime ("+[...] initialize may have
been in progress in another thread when fork() was called") or segfault once that
check is disabled. Both fork attempts of our PHerc1667 run died this way, while
earlier PHerc0139 runs were unaffected, so it is a race at fork time. "spawn" needs a picklable
dataset, and WindingModelDataset holds nanobind GridRaycaster objects (and
VolumeSlabExtractor holds vc.Volume handles) that cannot be pickled.

What: Segment drops its raycaster when pickled and rebuilds it from the grid when
unpickled; VolumeSlabExtractor drops its per-process volume handles (they already
reopen lazily); the trainer reads `dataloader_start_method` (default "fork",
unchanged behaviour).

Checked: on 8 PHerc0139 slabs drawn through spawn workers from the pickled dataset,
labels and images are identical to the fork path (scripts/check_villa_patches.py).
Limit: crossings-only patch packs (np.memmap) are pickled as full copies.

diff --git a/vesuvius/src/vesuvius/neural_tracing/winding_models/train_winding_model.py b/vesuvius/src/vesuvius/neural_tracing/winding_models/train_winding_model.py
index 25d2e99..1e05d10 100755
--- a/vesuvius/src/vesuvius/neural_tracing/winding_models/train_winding_model.py
+++ b/vesuvius/src/vesuvius/neural_tracing/winding_models/train_winding_model.py
@@ -419,7 +419,11 @@ def make_dataloader(dataset, config, *, generator, num_workers):
     if num_workers > 0:
         kwargs["persistent_workers"] = bool(config.get("persistent_workers", True))
         kwargs["prefetch_factor"] = max(1, int(config.get("prefetch_factor", 2)))
-        kwargs["multiprocessing_context"] = "fork"
+        # "fork" is fastest on Linux; macOS needs "spawn" (forked workers can
+        # abort in the Objective-C runtime).
+        kwargs["multiprocessing_context"] = str(
+            config.get("dataloader_start_method", "fork")
+        )
         # Draws are procedural, so batch order carries no meaning; letting
         # finished batches overtake a straggling worker keeps one slow draw
         # from stalling the rank (and with DDP, every other rank).
diff --git a/vesuvius/src/vesuvius/neural_tracing/winding_models/volume_slab_extractor.py b/vesuvius/src/vesuvius/neural_tracing/winding_models/volume_slab_extractor.py
